WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.267
-Michael B. Jordan!
-Man, I love coming here, man.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.567
I love it.
-Come on. You feel that...

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
You feel that love?!

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.400
Do you feel it? Come on.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.834
-I love it, I love it,
I love it, I love it.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.367
-They love you, buddy.
-I love coming here, man.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:14.534
This is a
great, great spot, man.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.434
-Well, we love having you here.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.501
You're hosting
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:18.767
-Yes, sir.
-How's it going, bud?

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.100
-It's going great.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.167
I literally just left,
you know, rehearsal just now,

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.834
going through the blocking
and stuff like that.

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:25.367
And it's a machine.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:28.467
And they are so fantastic and
great at what they do.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.234
It's been a great process.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.267
-Can you talk to me about
the pillow?

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:33.334
-Oh, yeah, the pillow.

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.801
Okay, so,
I walk into the office.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.701
And they're like,
"Alright, this might be weird.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:38.901
This might be a little weird.

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:40.033
We actually have been
living with you

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.200
for the last 10 years."

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.434
I said, "Living with me
the last 10 years?

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:43.834
What are you talking about?"

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:46.067
They're just like, "Well --"
It was one of the producer's

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:49.100
birthday, and it was --
one of the other employees

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.434
there got her a pillow, right?

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.901
And it was a life-sized,
almost like a pregnancy pillow

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:59.100
of me printed on both sides.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.267
And I'm like, "Wait.
You guys had this for how long?"

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:04.234
It's been there for 10 years.
It's been there for a decade.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.300
-You brought us a photo.
-I got a photo of it.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.968
And I'm like, "Wait a second."

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:12.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.501
So, I'm like,
"So, wait, wait, wait."

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:15.801
I said, "Whose pillow is that?"

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.801
And, you know, the lady was
like, "Oh, it's mine."

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.834
And she was like, "Listen,
our hours here are so crazy,

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.534
everybody takes naps, you know,
at some point during the day."

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.767
-Of course.
-I was like, "So wait.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.400
Every lady in here has slept
with me at some point

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.567
over the last 10 years?"

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.934
-That's exactly right.
-And they were like,

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.133
"Yes, actually, everybody has,
at one point."

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.767
-That's exactly right.
Yeah, why not?

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:33.934
-That was cool.

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:35.334
-I've got to say,

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.834
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever"
came out.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:41.000
There were rumors --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.267
It was fantastic.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.934
-There was rumors,
are you going to be in it?

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.200
Are you not going to be in it?

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.667
And when I saw you
in interviews, you were like,

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.634
"I am not in this at all."

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:52.767
If you have seen it
or plan on seeing it,

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:55.701
maybe just mute your TV
for a second.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.167
You are in it.
-Yeah, I am in it.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And it was great.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.534
-Thank you, thank you.
-It was awesome.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.267
How hard is it
to keep that secret?

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.968
-It's tough, you know?

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.634
I think, this time around,
you know,

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.400
because we lost our brother
Chadwick, you know --

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.901
Rest in peace to
Chadwick Boseman.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:16.667
And it was so much weight
and so much just

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.000
trying to power through,
you know?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.167
And Ryan Coogler
had such, you know,

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:22.767
a tremendous task in front of
him to evolve the script

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.267
and the story in a way that
still kind of honored Chadwick,

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.267
but move the franchise
forward, as well.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.701
So for me to be able to
come back, you know,

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.567
and I had to really keep it
under wraps, you know?

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:32.934
I had to grow my hair out.

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:35.601
You know, I got the locks back
in and stuff like that.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:37.567
And, you know,
I'm traveling a lot of places,

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.667
so I've got to, you know,
wear a hat, a hoodie, you know,

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:43.133
fly private,
which isn't too bad of a thing.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:46.601
But being able to keep it under
wraps was really a tough thing.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.634
-Were you doing "Creed III"
at the same time?

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.501
-Yeah, we were both shooting
down in Atlanta

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:51.567
at the same time.

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:52.734
So that made it
a little bit easier

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.601
to be able to bounce around
from studios.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:57.100
But it was a hard thing
to keep under wraps.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.400
-How do you do -- First of all,
you're not only starring in

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.734
"Creed III," you produced it,and
this is -- you directed it.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:05.167
-Mm-hmm.
-This is your directorial debut.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:06.300
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.634
-You crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:10.267
-You crushed it, buddy.
-Thank you, man, thank you.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:13.100
-How do you like
directing yourself?

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.200
-I love it.
You know, it's --

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.601
-You get along with yourself?
-Yeah, just a little bit.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.501
-I mean, the lead actor's
a bit of an ass[bleep]

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:19.567
but, you know, it's cool,
you know?

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:20.868
You know, we got through it.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.033
-Eventually, you got the
performance out of him, yeah.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.601
What's it like directing
with gloves on?

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:25.667
-It's tough.

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:26.767
You know, you're -- You know,

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:27.834
you've got a mouthpiece
in sometimes.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.000
You got gloves.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.634
You're always depending on
so many people.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.000
Your team is everything,
you know?

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.000
So, to be able to be in
the middle of a boxing scene,

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.300
honestly, it's sometimes easier,
because I can direct

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.634
while I'm acting.

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:41.000
You know, if I needed to move
you upstage a little bit,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.367
I just move
a little bit like this

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:43.901
and then I get the shot
that I need,

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:45.834
'cause I'm already -- I'm kind
of I'm low-key cheating,

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.434
'cause I'm, like, editing while
I'm actually acting

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:48.868
a little bit.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.601
-Yeah, all of a sudden, you just
start moving around the scene.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.701
Wow, yeah,
you're finding your light.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.200
-So, it's -- Yeah,
so it was fun. It was fun.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.467
-Did you get to talk to any
other directors beforehand?

00:03:58.467 --> 00:03:59.934
-Reached out to
a lot of directors.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.868
You know, I'm blessed to have,
you know,

00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:06.701
Denzel Washington, Ryan Coogler,
Steven Caple, Jon Favreau,

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:08.200
Bradley Cooper, you know?

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.300
Like, I reached out to, like,
the community of directors,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.567
and everybody gave me
great advice.

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:15.300
And one of the greatest advices
I got was from

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.534
Bradley Cooper and Jon Favreau.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.467
They was basically like,
"Get your first shot off

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.000
as quickly as possible."

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.167
Like, it's one of the --
it's one of the --

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.400
It can slow down
your entire day.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.968
You know, if you don't get that
first shot off very early,

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.934
you're probably not
going to make your day.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.501
So as soon as you get it off,
the train is rolling

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:33.033
and the machine just won't stop,
so you'll more than likely

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:34.200
get more shots than you --

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.667
-I love that advice.
-Yeah.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.400
-That's good.
-Thank you.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:42.000
-You know, I watch
these movies and I go,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.400
"There's no way
they can make the shots

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.968
look different
in a boxing ring."

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:46.968
You did it again.

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.234
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you.

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:50.434
-It's something else -- It feels
like you're in the ring.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:53.033
Like, I've never --
Again, I've seen, you know,

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.934
the "Rockys,"
I've seen the "Creeds."

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.133
But what was the -- This thing
was, like -- It's insane.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.667
You actually see
skin flapping and blob.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.567
I go -- How did you
change the game again?

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.067
-We were just --
You know, I think I got --

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:06.567
It was a gift
and a curse, you know?

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:07.901
There's been, you know,
eight other movies before me,

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.067
you know?

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.200
And we've shot --
You can shoot a boxing match

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.667
so many different ways.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.400
I think 'cause I was
kind of put in a corner,

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.734
it kind of forced me to be more
creative and really find --

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.267
like, think outside the box
of how to make

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:20.367
the fights different.

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:22.033
So we shot
all the fights in IMAX.

00:05:22.033 --> 00:05:25.100
And, also, I had a huge
Japanese anime influence

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.300
on a lot of my fighters.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.100
I'm an anime nerd, so...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:32.968
I found unique ways to
kind of -- Exactly.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.300
Yeah, you --
-And then -- Dude, it was --

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.567
-The thing and the thing?
Okay, alright.

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.968
-Yeah. But I watched as a fan.
I'm just enjoying.

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:39.033
You put the work in, man.
-Yes, sir.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:40.934
-I was like,
"Oh, it was great."

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:41.968
Jonathan Majors, by the way,
is who you go up against.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:44.934
-Ooh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.100
-Dude...
-My brother is incredible, man.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.467
-Dude is jacked in this movie.
-Yes, he is.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:50.734
-Both of you guys are.
-My man's in shape.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.667
I thought, you --
I go, "Oh, my God.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.434
That's Michael B. Jordan."

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.634
Then he shows --
Get ready, 'cause he shows up,

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:57.968
and I'm like, "Wow!"

00:05:57.968 --> 00:06:01.734
-He is in the most insane shape
that I've ever seen.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.167
And we needed somebody that was
going to be, you know,

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:06.701
an antagonist,
but somebody intimidating.

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:08.534
We wanted to make Adonis
feel like an underdog.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.834
So when you see Jonathan Majors,

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:12.267
he looks like he can
beat the crap out of whoever.

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:13.367
-Yeah.
-Uh-huh.

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:14.834
-Yeah, and he
plays it perfectly,

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:18.300
'cause you feel for him
and then you don't.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.167
Then you -- He's a punk.
-You know, I mean --

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.300
-Then you're like,
I want you to win, you know?

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.801
-I think it's more interesting
to have, like,

00:06:23.801 --> 00:06:25.467
an antagonist
that has depth to him.

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:27.667
Like, he's not just a,
you know, twirl the mustache,

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:28.701
"Ha, ha, I'm a bad guy."

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:30.167
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.267
-You've got to understand, you
know, why he is the way he is.

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:33.801
-It was well done.
-Thank you.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:34.834
-How do we set this up,
"Creed III"?

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:35.901
-"Creed III."

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:37.501
I think it's about, you know,

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:38.934
you can't really outrun
your past.

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:41.100
You know, you have to kind of
like, look inward to,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.267
you know, to -- And you have to
face your demons

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:44.501
in order to move forward
in life.

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:45.834
You know, you can't just
keep moving forward

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:47.934
without actually reflecting.

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:49.501
I think, you know,
childhood trauma,

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.667
those transformative years,
things that you've been through,

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:53.200
you have to face those
things in order to

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.000
have the courage to
move forward to do new things.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.534
And I think that's
a big part of our film.

00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:05.534
-And Adonis Creed sees someone
from his past that was --

00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:07.067
It was one of his old buddies.

00:07:07.067 --> 00:07:09.100
And he just returns
and he is trouble, man.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.400
-He's trouble.
-He's trouble.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.067
-He turns Adonis' world
upside down,

00:07:12.067 --> 00:07:14.901
and he has to kind of
move backwards to move forward.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:16.100
-Checkmate.
-My man.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.834
-You know what I'm saying?
-Ooh! Checkmate.

00:07:17.834 --> 00:07:20.133
-You know what I'm saying?
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:22.167
Here's Michael B. Jordan
in "Creed III."

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.534
Take a look at this.

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.934
-Hey, my man.

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:28.801
Can I help you?

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:30.434
-Let me get an autograph?

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:31.801
-No, I ain't signing
no autographs,

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:32.801
but you get off of my car.

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:38.501
-Old homie.

00:07:38.501 --> 00:07:39.701
You don't remember me, huh?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.000
Come a long way from
bummin' rides from your mom.

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:47.968
-Dame.

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.567
Whew! Boy, you had --
you had -- you had me.

00:07:49.567 --> 00:07:51.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:53.701
-Damian.

00:07:53.701 --> 00:07:55.033
-Yeah, just got back
to the hood.

00:07:55.033 --> 00:07:57.033
Stopped by the old gym,
but, uh --

00:07:57.033 --> 00:07:59.634
-Yeah, we upgraded
a couple years ago.

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:01.234
-I see.

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:05.200
-Damn, it's -- it's, uh --

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.534
-It's been a minute.

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:09.300
-Been a minute.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.467
-Whoo!
-Yes.

00:08:10.467 --> 00:08:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Michael B. Jordan!

00:08:12.634 --> 00:08:17.367
"Creed III" is in theaters
and IMAX March 3rd.

00:08:17.367 --> 00:08:19.601
Michael is hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:08:19.601 --> 00:08:22.133
this weekend with musical guest
Lil Baby.

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:23.501
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:24.634
Come on back.

